{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1453777-pacts-of-ensorcellment","id":1453777,"title":"Pacts of Ensorcellment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-29T12:15:58-07:00","id":1453777,"title":"Pacts of Ensorcellment","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A retooled revival of a 1st edition mechanic I was fond of. Perhaps, as that book-nerd says, the ending has not yet been written.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well of course you want your loved ones to know. The truth is horrible, but it will set us free, and maybe keep us safe from the things that go bump in the night. Can you trust them with all that beautiful madness, though? Can you trust yourself to make that decision for them? Better make them swear on it.<br /> <br /> A particular variation on a bargain, a changeling can invest Glamour in a mortal\u2019s promise in order to allow them to peer beyond the veil that separates their world and the fae. It\u2019s trivially easy to accomplish, but can be waterfall-leapingly difficult to follow through on. Showing your heart is always difficult.<br /> <br /> To ensorcell a mortal, the changeling must first extract a promise. Unlike a bargain\u2019s tit-for-tat dealings, the promise of ensorcellment is usually more open-ended. Traditionally the Lost demand their charge swear never to tell anyone about what they see. Also common are declarations of love, loyalty, friendship, and all that other gunk that makes the bad guys in children\u2019s cartoons retch. \u201cPromise not to freak out?\u201d is common enough for the more casual elf, but tends to get broken pretty quickly. Regardless, the Wyrd needs some sort of promise as the base.<br /> <br /> Next, the Lost has a choice: Ensorcell the mortal directly, or ensorcell an object.<br /> <br /> In the former case, the pact is sealed with some sort of symbolic gesture: a handshake, a kiss on the lips, placing a mask over the mortal\u2019s face, a thwack on the back of the head. Whatever the changeling\u2019s feeling. In parts of Finland they use spruce branches. Regardless, a point of Glamour must be spent. So long as the mortal keeps their end of the promise, they gain the ability to see through the Mask as if they were a changeling.<br /> <br /> In the latter, the changeling chooses some small object to receive the Glamour, such as a lucky penny or a stone with a hole running through it. The ensorcellment works as above, but the mortal must keep the object on their person in order to see through the Mask. Sometimes merely having the item in pocket is enough, while other times a mortal may need to peer through a spyglass lens, wear a bracelet, or hold their finger on the trigger of a revolver in order for the enchantment to take effect. The changeling either defines the conditions for the sight, or can elect to leave it up to the Wyrd. The object only works for the intended mortal, though a changeling can key multiple promise-swearers to the same item. Magic that identifies tokens will identify the enchanted object as a token so long as it holds Glamour.<br /> <br /> In either method, if the mortal breaks their end of the deal, the ensorcellment immediately ends, the Mask quickly falling back over their perceptions. The changeling does not need to swear any promise on their end: The Glamour they provide counts for that. At any time, they may snatch the Glamour back if they can touch the enchanted mortal or object, returning it to their own pool and ending the ensorcellment early. This <i>does</i> count as breaking a pledge, however. If the mortal is reaped by any character, the Glamour is also lost.<br /> <br /> While ensorcelled, witnessing fae phenomena does provoke Integrity Breaking Points (at least not on their face: Watching a Gristlegrinder make mincemeat out of some poor hobgoblin is still an unnerving experience). This extends to changelings dropping the Mask as well: The mortal does not become Spooked from observing the act.<br /> <br /> If the changeling chooses, they may spend additional Glamour and Willpower to make the ensorcellment double as a sealing.<br /> <br /> Any acts the ensorcelled mortal takes that would cause a Clarity attack on the part of the ensorcelling changeling add one die to both the attack and damage roll. Betrayal from those who know the truth hurts that much more.<br /> <br /> After ensorcellment ends, whether naturally or through the breaking of the pledge or theft of Glamour, the mortal\u2019s memories of everything they experienced become hazy, detached, and dreamlike. They must succeed on a Wits + Composure roll, penalized by half the ensorcelling changeling\u2019s Wyrd rating (rounded up) or gain the Amnesia Condition related to fae interactions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}